[E-REWRITE-REPEATEDLY-RULE] Error: this rule would rewrite forever
   ╭─[ reject/rewrite-repeatedly-rule-loops.sw:8:64 ]
   │
 8 │ theorem bad ∀ (x y: Nat): x + y = y + x := rewrite repeatedly [Nat.addComm]
   │                                                                ─────┬─────  
   │                                                                     ╰─────── it rewrites `_ + _` to `_ + _`, which it fits again
   │ 
   │ Note 1: its right side holds an instance of its left side, so each rewrite makes another place it applies
   │ 
   │ Note 2: use it once with `rewrite`, with its arguments given; reordering a sum or product is `algebra`'s or `arithmetic`'s job
───╯
